diff --git a/doc/changelog.d/0.fixed.md b/doc/changelog.d/0.fixed.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4723a34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/changelog.d/0.fixed.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Report incomplete snapshot reads in ``compare_files`` instead of treating matching errors or omitted state as equal case settings. Add optional exact settings-path value comparisons. Collect the two cases in separate, sequential temporary sessions to avoid requiring two concurrent Fluent licences. Use headless launches, the lightweight file-read command, and the available run-calculation settings group.
diff --git a/doc/source/user_guide/tools_and_capabilities.rst b/doc/source/user_guide/tools_and_capabilities.rst
index 599b928..3c94e2c 100644
--- a/doc/source/user_guide/tools_and_capabilities.rst
+++ b/doc/source/user_guide/tools_and_capabilities.rst
@@ -123,6 +123,20 @@ Route all "show mesh quality / skewness / check mesh" intents to
 without touching the live workspace session. Requires the ``file-probe`` extra for
 ``.h5``/``.cas.h5`` files.
 
+If a snapshot read fails or its state is omitted by the size limit, the tool returns
+``{"error": "comparison incomplete", "detail": {...}}``. The details identify the
+affected input (``path_a`` or ``path_b``), section or settings path, and read error.
+No difference count or comparison summary is returned for incomplete snapshots.
+The two temporary Fluent sessions run one after the other and are closed by the tool.
+
+Pass optional ``settings_paths`` (up to 10 exact Fluent settings paths) to compare
+values beyond the default global state and named-object names. For example, a
+named inlet's velocity can be checked with
+``settings_paths=["setup/boundary-conditions/velocity-inlet[cold-inlet]/momentum/velocity-magnitude/value"]``.
+The result lists the selected paths, and any changed value appears in the normal
+diff and summary. A requested path that cannot be read makes the comparison
+incomplete.
+
 Workflow examples
 -----------------
 
